domain ADR0030B4ActionPlan:
  description "Choose the bounded local implementation shape for ADR-0030 B4 durable attempts and preservation."

problem P1:
  |
    Accepted ADR-0030 and plan task cb204 require durable frozen migration
    attempts, individually identified provider requests, restricted bounded
    preservation capsules, disclosure controls, and crash/retry fixtures before
    semantic generation and repair orchestration are implemented.

evidence E_REQUIREMENT:
  |
    ADR-0030 D5, D6 and D10 require a 256 KiB content-digested capsule outside
    ordinary compilers, immutable attempt identity over source and provider
    inputs, distinct providerRequestId receipts, and replay without duplicate
    provider work. Requirement R9 says provider failure leaves the current
    generation unchanged and the attempt retryable.

evidence E_SEQUENCE:
  |
    Plan cb204 precedes cb205 semantic change-set generation and repair, cb206
    structural enforcement, cb207 semantic review, and cb208 owner acceptance.
    B4 therefore must not invent or deliver those later behaviors.

evidence E_CURRENT:
  |
    The repository already has immutable asset_generations, CAS activation, a
    SQLite bootstrap schema in backend/src/db.ts, ordered PostgreSQL migrations,
    transaction helpers, canonical JSON hashing, and isolated SQLite repository
    tests. It has no character semantic migration attempt, provider-request, or
    preservation-capsule tables or repository.

premise P_BOUNDARY:
  |
    B4 is local implementation only. It does not authorize provider calls,
    production data writes, V3 generation activation, authoring-policy cutover,
    deployment, or migration of any character.

premise P_APPEND:
  |
    Append-oriented persistence is most directly represented by immutable base
    records and separate append-only event or receipt records. Updating a single
    status or response column would obscure crash and retry history.

premise A1:
  "Alternative: extend character_authoring_attempts with migration columns and mutable status fields."

premise A2:
  "Alternative: add dedicated immutable attempt and provider-request records, append-only events and receipts, and a separately restricted capsule repository."

premise A3:
  "Alternative: define schemas and in-memory fixtures only, deferring physical persistence."

decision D1 based_on P1, E_REQUIREMENT, E_SEQUENCE, E_CURRENT, P_BOUNDARY, P_APPEND, A1, A2, A3:
  |
    Select A2. Add shared strict schemas for frozen attempt inputs, disclosure
    grants, request identity, receipts, events, and preservation capsules. Add a
    forward-only PostgreSQL migration and matching SQLite bootstrap tables. Add
    one repository that inserts immutable attempt and request bases, appends
    events and one terminal receipt per request, replays exact identities,
    rejects identity drift, enforces the six-request ceiling and 256 KiB capsule
    limit, and exposes capsule reads only through the registered future-migration
    consumer API. Verify exact replay, crash resume, failure retry, disclosure
    rejection, capsule bounds, and absence of asset-generation/current-pointer
    writes. Do not add semantic operations, provider invocation, candidate merge,
    owner acceptance, activation, or policy cutover in B4.

premise LIMIT:
  |
    Passing local fixtures will establish storage and retry mechanics only. It
    will not establish provider semantic quality, complete migration validation,
    production migration safety, deployment readiness, or restored characters.
